1
00:00:00,531 --> 00:00:04,471
(Howard:)No, but I did go
to the International Space Station.

2
00:00:04,635 --> 00:00:06,005
(Girl:)Did you fly the rocket?

3
00:00:07,004 --> 00:00:10,304
(Howard:)No, but I was in the rocket.

4
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:12,638
(Howard:)- I didn't actually...
- So you just flew around?

5
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:15,300
(Girl:)That's kind of like my uncle.
A flight attendant.

6
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:24,040
No, heh, I'm an American hero,
your uncle brings people nuts, okay?

7
00:00:24,221 --> 00:00:25,811
All right, all right, all right.

8
00:00:26,023 --> 00:00:30,123
(Leonard:)Boy, we are learning a lot here, huh?
Thank you, Astronaut Howard.

9
00:00:31,495 --> 00:00:34,155
(Leonard:)Um, I am what's called
an experimental physicist.

10
00:00:34,331 --> 00:00:39,231
Which is super fun because I get
to test theories and work with lasers.

11
00:00:39,837 --> 00:00:42,667
(Leonard:)- Yes?
- How did you decide to become a scientist?

12
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,170
Oh, excellent question.

13
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:47,831
(Leonard:)Um, I suppose I've always been into science.

14
00:00:48,045 --> 00:00:52,105
(Leonard:)My mother and father are scientists,
so I was kind of led in that direction.

15
00:00:52,283 --> 00:00:54,653
(Leonard:)Pushed might be a better way to describe it.

16
00:00:55,586 --> 00:01:00,026
(Leonard:)To be honest with you guys, when
I was your age, I wanted to be a rap star.

